return {h=12,w=250,cr=75,hc=20,bh=70,gr="medium",eg={"water1","dragon"},st={55,65,95,95,45,85},ab={{38,0},{97,0},{6,1}},genus={en="Dragon Pokémon",es="Pokémon Dragón",pt="Pokémon Dragão"},flavor={en={[1]="Capable of swimming backwards by rapidly flapping its wing-like pectoral fins and stout tail.",[2]="Capable of swimming backwards by rapidly flapping its wing-like pectoral fins and stout tail.",[3]="Touching the back fin causes numbness. It hooks its tail to coral to stay in place while sleeping.",[4]="An examination of its cells revealed the presence of a gene not found in HORSEA. It became a hot topic.",[5]="Its fin-tips leak poison. Its fins and bones are highly valued as ingredients in herbal medicine.",[6]="The male raises the young. If it is approached, it uses its toxic spikes to fend off the intruder.",[7]="SEADRA sleeps after wriggling itself between the branches of coral. Those trying to harvest coral are occasionally stung by this Pokémon’s poison barbs if they fail to notice it.",[8]="SEADRA generates whirlpools by spinning its body. The whirlpools are strong enough to swallow even fishing boats. This Pokémon weakens prey with these currents, then swallows it whole.",[9]="The poisonous barbs all over its body are highly valued as ingredients for making traditional herbal medicine. It shows no mercy to anything approaching its nest.",[10]="Its body bristles with sharp spikes. Carelessly trying to touch it could cause fainting from the spikes.",[11]="It is capable of swimming backwards by rapidly flapping its winglike pectoral fins and stout tail.",[12]="Its spines provide protection. Its fins and bones are prized as traditional medicine ingredients.",[13]="Its spines provide protection. Its fins and bones are prized as traditional medicine ingredients.",[14]="Its spines provide protection. Its fins and bones are prized as traditional medicine ingredients.",[15]="An examination of its cells revealed the presence of a gene not found in HORSEA. It became a